# /etc/sysusers.d/obsd.conf — who the archive's engine runs as, and the group its clients join.
# Installed and applied by install-obsd.sh (`systemd-sysusers`); read again by systemd at every boot.
# ================================================================================================
# NOTES — what every part of this file does and why (kept beside the code, not in a separate document)
# ================================================================================================
# # obsd.sysusers — the user and the group `vms-obsd`, which obsd.service names
#
# **Role.** `obsd.service` runs the daemon as `User=vms-obsd`, `Group=vms-obsd` and lets in, besides its own user,
# only the members of `OBSD_CLIENT_GROUP=vms-obsd` — the recorders. A unit that names a user nobody created does not
# start (217/USER), and without the daemon nothing is recorded (the review's fourth pass, blocker 2): this file
# creates both, the way the box creates every system user it needs.
#
# - `g vms-obsd 2101` — the group with a FIXED number. The recorder runs in a container, which has no /etc/group of
#   the host's: it joins the group by number (`GroupAdd=2101` in `recworker@.container`, the Nomad job's `user`
#   in М11). `install-obsd.sh` refuses a box where `vms-obsd` already exists with another number.
# - `u vms-obsd -:vms-obsd` — the daemon's own user, a system one with no login, whose primary group is that one:
#   what the daemon writes (the socket, the volumes' files) is `vms-obsd:vms-obsd`.
#
# The names are the product's (its install.sh, `useradd --system --user-group vms-obsd`): ObjectStorage is the VMS's
# archive engine, not the platform's, and keeps the VMS's names. One group is the daemon's and its clients' alike —
# the course had two, the user `obsd` and the clients' group `vms-rec`, until it took the product's.
# ================================================================================================
g vms-obsd 2101           -
u vms-obsd -:vms-obsd     "ObjectStorage daemon (obsd.service)" - -
